column37:
I don't know if this will fit your needs, but couchdb is pretty fast.  It's under active development and still alpha, so things do change.  As for multi-key, it's a yes and no sort of situation.<p>If you want to do an intersection you can, unfortunately it's in a sorted order.
for example: [key1, key2, key3] won't match [key2,key1, key3]<p>If you're trying just get all images matching a key so your structure looks like:<p><pre><code>  {img (url, binaray, etc), tags: [tag1, tag2, tag3, tag4]}
</code></pre>
you can run a simple map function over the data<p><pre><code>  function map (doc)
  {
    for each (var tag in tags)
       emit (tag, null);
  }
</code></pre>
which will allow you to then get all images by tag:<p><pre><code>  key=tag
</code></pre>
It doesn't have a c++ api, but it  uses http as its interface so you can use curl..
